{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988390-temenos-realm-dharmakshetra-and-the-duel-goetic","id":988390,"title":"[Temenos Realm] Dharmakshetra and the Duel Goetic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T14:17:12-07:00","id":988390,"title":"[Temenos Realm] Dharmakshetra and the Duel Goetic","content":"Here's some stuff I've been working on that will hopefully make its way into my chronicle, but I thought other people might enjoy it too. Let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Dharmakshetra</b>, the Field of Righteousness, is a Temenos realm linked to the Duel Arcane and the ideal of magical combat as a perfect clash between the souls of the Awakened. It appears as a compound built into a mountain rising above the clouds, a winding series of chambers and balconies and precarious cliffsides, any of which would make for a scenic location for a fight. Every chamber has its own aesthetic, and much like the Metropolis, the architectural and natural styles of different eras and regions blend together. One chamber resembles a Roman gladiatorial amphitheatre in its prime, another resembles the courtyard of a Shaolin monastery, another is a string of rocky floating platforms held together by heavy chains, and yet another is very obviously modeled on the island fortress from <i>Enter the Dragon</i>.<br /> <br /> The realm has very few native inhabitants, only the silent Castellans and the ever-circling Rocs. The entire place seems hauntingly empty, like walking through a ruin from a lost civilization. Indeed, some mages believe that the realm is an outpost from the Time Before, an Atlantean temple to martial glory that endured the Fall in some capacity. Others see it as &quot;merely&quot; a Temenos realm reflecting the Duel Arcane itself, changing and shifting over time with the dreams of combative mages. Mages who investigate the matter further (perhaps as an Obsession) will find significant evidence that Dharmakshetra is the abandoned Temenos realm of a fallen Legacy that centered on the Duel Arcane- but what happened to them?<br /> <br /> The Field of Righteousness has few natives, but it does have visitors. Mages from all over the world who have learned about this hidden realm, many of them Adamantine Arrows or Mystagogues, travel here to spar with like-minded duelists near and far. It is not uncommon to encounter the Astral form of another mage on a given visit to the realm. Some mages plan to meet a rival here to settle their grievance in a private and aesthetically pleasing environment, while others just hope to encounter a challenger from a Consilium on the other side of the world for a friendly(?) test of skill. The various chambers are equipped with every mundane weapon and armament a duelist could wish for, and practicing in this realm is a great justification for raising Weaponry, Firearms, Athletics, or Brawl.<br /> <br /> The spell &quot;Display of Power&quot; functions slightly differently in Dharmakshetra: the Imagos of the duelists are vividly realized, and can be seen by any observer, even without Mage Sight active. If the spell risks Paradox, the pool is at a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> Having a private magical space for the Duel Arcane is nice enough, but for many mages who know about this secret realm, the main draw is a challenge mostly unique to it: the Duel Goetic. This rare and deeply personal form of magical combat pits the Oneiric forms of the duelists' virtues and flaws against one another, empowered by their Arcana. It has been compared to the variant form of the Duel Arcane known as Shadow Chess, and seems to have been developed along similar lines, but it has its own quirks. The dueling space is almost always created by the Influence of a compliant Castellan rather than a mage's own spells. Engaging in the Duel Goetic earns both duelists an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>The Duel Goetic </b>consists of two mages using special Goetia drawn from their own Oneiros to attack each other indirectly. Two are summoned from each duelist: one representing a strength or virtue called an Exemplar, another representing a weakness or vice called an Iniquity. They need not represent the mage's actual Virtue or Vice trait; look to Aspirations, Obsessions, and Conditions for inspiration as well as the character's background. The relevant aspects of the mage's personality are weaker and less deeply felt while conjured up, although watching one's Hope being literally crushed can still provoke an emotional reaction. By the terms of the duel, each duelist controls his own Exemplar and his opponent's Iniquity.<br /> <br /> Each mage chooses one Arcanum to act as her Sword during the duel. Depending on the terms, each duelist might choose their own highest Arcanum, or their own lowest, or they might both use the same Arcanum regardless of relative rating.<br /> <br /> The duelists do not attack each other directly. Instead, they direct and support their Goetia, who attack and use Numina on the rival mage and each other. All parties may move around the battlefield and apply Defense as normal, and mages may activate their Amnions and Mage Armor unless the terms of the duel specify otherwise. When a mage would take damage from an attack, she can reflexively shunt all damage to the Corpus of one Goetia she controls, taking any excess damage herself beyond what would discorporate it. When a Goetia discorporates, it returns to the Oneiros of its originating mage.<br /> <br /> Initiative is determined based on the mage's Finesse+Resistance, as they are in dream form. Goetia act on their controlling mage's initiative count, with Exemplars acting before Iniquities. The summoned Goetia cannot act independently, only when they are actively controlled by a mage on their turn.<br /> <br /> Like the Duel Arcane, duelists use an Attribute rather than Gnosis in their dicepool. Each turn, a mage may take one of the following actions depending on her Sword rating. All spells must account for spell factors (especially Scale if targeting two or more Goetia) and Withstand ratings as normal. The mage may not use Yantras or spend Reach beyond the free Reach granted by her Arcanum rating, but she may spend Willpower to add dice or spend Mana one-for-one (following her Gnosis-based limit) to access additional Reach effects.<ul><li>Sword 1: cast &quot;Know Spirit&quot; using Finesse+Sword</li> <li>Sword 2: cast &quot;Command Spirit&quot; using Power+Sword, although it cannot use Advanced Duration. One Potency gives one Goetia one command.</li> <li>Sword 3: cast &quot;Bolster Spirit&quot; using Resistance+Sword</li> <li>Sword 3: cast &quot;Damage Ghost&quot; using Power+Sword</li> <li>Sword 4: cast &quot;Shape Spirit&quot; using Finesse+Sword</li> <li>Sword 5: cast &quot;Birth Spirit&quot; using Resistance+Sword, which can represent any Goetia the caster wishes, although it cannot use Advanced Duration</li> </ul><br /> By default, the Duel Goetic ends when one duelist loses all her Goetia or her dream form is destroyed, whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> When they are first conjured, Exemplars and Iniquities are Rank 1 and Size 5. They have Power 2, Finesse 2, Resistance 2, Influence 1 related to their nature, Essence 10, Willpower 4, and one Numen. Ban: can only act when commanded by a mage. Bane: any Castellan. Appropriate Numina include: Awe, Blast, Dement, Drain, Emotional Aura, Entropic Decay, Regenerate, Speed, and Stalwart.<br /> <br /> It is possible to use Command Spirit to control an opponent's Goetia or Shape Spirit to change any Goetia's Ban and Bane, but doing so is against the rules of the realm and will cause the nearest Castellan (if they sense it with Power+Finesse) to break up the duel before silently returning to their post.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> More stuff is coming. Thoughts so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:43:52-07:00","id":988469,"title":"","content":"There are a number of ways to access Dharmakshetra, although it helps to know that it exists in the first place.<br /> <br /> If one has been invited by a mage who already knows the place, the host may use a Ruling Mind spell called Astral Beacon to make the realm obvious when the invited steps off their Astral Path into the Temenos.<br /> <br /> Supposedly, meditating in the presence of an active Duel Arcane in which at least one duelist has been to the Field of Righteousness counts as a Synese that leads to the realm directly. Fulfilling those conditions safely is an exercise for the reader.<br /> <br /> Various texts from centuries past in the libraries of the Adamantine Arrow and the Mysterium describe Dharmakshetra in vivid enough terms that an Astral traveler can go searching for it. There is also a similarly effective VHS-based Grimoire titled &quot;Peach Blossom Paradise, Vol. 2&quot; circulated among the Free Council which intercuts footage from various pre-1999 kung fu and wuxia films, demonstrating the magical power in their shared imagery of an otherworldly &quot;fighting paradise.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Peach Blossom Paradise, Vol. 2 (Grimoire </b>\u2022\u2022<b>)</b><br /> Prime 3 &quot;Display of Power&quot; [Brawl], Mind 3 &quot;Goetic Summons&quot; [Streetwise], Mind 3 &quot;Enhance Skill&quot; [Expression], and one rote related to Astral travel.<br /> <br /> Viewing the video in its entirety (76 minutes, various languages, English subtitles) grants +2 on any rolls to navigate to Dharmakshetra in the Temenos, and frequently creates a relevant Obsession. </div> </div> </div>---<br /> <br /> <b>Castellans </b>are the most obvious native inhabitants of Dharmakshetra, although there are not many of them (left?) and they try to be inconspicuous. They resemble living bronze statues of humans with gemstone eyes, long, elastic limbs and colorful but practical linen clothes. All of them carry an ornamental melee weapon, usually of South Indian origin. They never speak or write, although they have been known to subvocalize, but they understand High Speech and most languages spoken in the Buddhist world historically, and will sometimes point to written inscriptions on the walls.<br /> <br /> When they are encountered, they are either wandering the compound (they usually stick to the interior and certain balconies) on some duty or standing watch over a specific chamber, silently observing without judgment. If asked for directions to a certain chamber or place of interest inside the compound, they will usually lead the mage there personally. There are some locations high on the mountain or behind sealed doors that they will simply refuse to lead visitors to, and return to their business as if nothing happened.<br /> <br /> If they are attacked maliciously, they are skilled combatants, but do not seek to &quot;kill&quot; and will stop fighting and return to their business if the aggressor is incapacitated or backs off. Some experienced visitors claim to have studied certain inscriptions deeper in the compound and learned how to spar with the Castellans as a friendly test of skill that begins and ends with a bow.<br /> <br /> The greatest use of a Castellan for most mages is their ability to prepare a chamber for the Duel Goetic using their Influence 3 (Dueling) to Control. They are willing to do so if asked and both participants are present, but there is always a price. The mages must state the terms of the duel, including a sacrifice for the defeated party. Suitable sacrifices range from dedicating one's next victory in the Duel Arcane to Dharmakshetra (which prevents the Triumphant Condition), to handing over an Imbued Item, to revealing one's sympathetic name, to remaining in Dharmakshetra until the mage defeats someone else in the Duel Goetic. At least one miserable soul has died in the physical world without being able to wake up or defeat an opponent.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in the Field of Righteousness is a Rote that lets mages activate the Duel Goetic themselves without need for a Castellan. But will they give the rote to a mage that earns their trust, or will it have to be copied from some hidden Grimoire in a forbidden chamber, or will the mage have to wrestle it from a third party?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Rocs </b>are the heavenly giant birds that dwell above the clouds and roost on the Dharmakshetra mountain. They mostly leave mages be, but they will swoop and attack any who try to fly or levitate up the mountain rather than passing through the chambers on foot. They don't like it when they catch you teleporting, either.<br /> <br /> If one can gain a Roc's trust and/or give it a suitable gift, they are willing to let a mage ride them as a passenger, and take them where they want to go within the realm or perhaps elsewhere in the Temenos. This is a great way to access the higher chambers that the Castellans (or other parties) forbid access to.<br /> <br /> A Roc's jeweled tail feather is a treasure with many uses in the Astral Realms, but one would surely earn the enmity of all Rocs if it were plucked rather than freely given.<br /> <br /> When the clouds grow stormy, Garuda, divine king of the Rocs, flies into aerial battle against the chthonic serpent Naga in a symbolic reflection of the realm's combative nature. Heaven help the mage foolish enough to duel outside during these fights. And yet, it could be a valuable insight into the mythology and magical theories of the fallen Legacy that seemingly originated Dharmakshetra, if one could only get close enough to study the duel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:57:45-07:00","id":988478,"title":"","content":"I really like the description of the realm. Lots of potential story hooks hiding in there, from finding a thing hidden on the site to finding connections to other strange realms.<br /> <br /> (Don't honestly care about the weird dueling rules, much, so I just skimmed them. No offense or anything---Just didn't hook me. I suppose that's feedback, too...)<br /> <br /> The Naga/Garuda duel is pretty slick. I would watch that.<br /> (Ho, okay: Imagine a Free Councilor who saw this and thought that it was both edifying and awesome to watch, so set about to stream it live. There's a weird plot hook, even if the two dueling don't actually care, since other magi almost certainly would be offended. Another would be to find out which parts fit which party's dominion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-16-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:06:25-07:00","id":989479,"title":"","content":"Why spend more time in Dharmakshetra than the Duration of a Duel Goetic? For its secrets, of course. Whether it is the Legacy realm of a fallen lineage of ancient duelists or a built-over ruin of the Time Before, there is surely lore (and treasure, and Arcane Beats) to be found here. Even if it's simply an emergent realm that only looks ancient, the visitors have brought interesting baggage with them.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Whether they founded the realm or merely adopted it, curious mages have determined that there is definitely a link between the Field of Righteousness and a certain <b>vanished Legacy</b>. There are consistent High Speech runes and revealing inscriptions in the deeper parts of the compound, and the Castellans are specifically aware of the Awakened and their customs in a way that suggests they were created by mages. Here is what has been uncovered with some certainty:<ul><li>The Legacy was open to any Path, but seems to have favored Mastigos.</li> <li>They had unusual Attainments, many of them related to mundane combat and the Duel Arcane, and favored Prime and Mind.</li> <li>They had great knowledge of goetia and shaping the Temenos, and probably created the Duel Goetic.</li> <li>They had a highly developed internal structure based on ranks which were climbed through challenging one's superior.</li> <li>They had low-level members from the Adamantine Arrow, but did not consider themselves friends of the Diamond. They claim that the Diamond feared and respected them. It is unclear whether or not they were considered Left-Handed.</li> <li>Their members felt that they were virtuous and justified, and went to great lengths to emphasize this in their writings, perhaps in response to outside criticism.</li> <li>They were closely integrated with Sleeper warrior cultures and martial societies.</li> <li>The Legacy seems to have been most popular and coherent in East Asia before about 900 CE, at which point it died out. However, it was rediscovered by small groups in several times and places over the centuries, from Nameless ronin in the Tokugawa period to German Arrow mercenaries in the Thirty Years' War, only to invariably die out within a generation.</li> <li>Knowledge of the Legacy seems to have been passed along by accessing Dharmakshetra itself.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Somewhere, secreted away in one of the hidden chambers of the compound, there must be a soul stone or daimonomikon of the fallen Legacy. And from there, sympathetic connections to anything else they left behind in the Astral or Fallen Worlds. Maybe the Legacy could even be revived! Things will be different this time!<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> A small but dedicated group of mages stalks the chambers of Dharmakshetra, Obsessed with uncovering its secrets and reclaiming the fallen Legacy. The <b>Dreamhounds </b>are a Nameless Order of Astral seekers and ruthless duelists who are scattered across the waking world, but come together in dreams to share information and pursue their mutual Obsession. They know the realm intimately and claim it as their own, disappearing into secret passages, whispering codewords to Castellans to secure their aid, riding on subservient Rocs to harry enemy mages and access hidden chambers, and descending to stranger places below the clouds where the great serpent Naga curls in wait. They are usually hostile to outsiders, although they can often be persuaded to resolve disputes with a formal Duel rather than open conflict.<br /> <br /> The Dreamhounds are easily recognized by virtue of their distinctive dream-bodies. Having taught each other secret ways to access the Astral, their self-image is shaped into a tall and prowling and vaguely canine thing (hence the name given to them by observers) that usually wears a colorful blindfold over its ink-black eyes. The great danger of the Dreamhounds is their expertise in Astral magic and their viciousness in preying on unwary visitors. They have access to an insidious Artifact known as an Astral Bubble, which (when thrown using Finesse+Athletics-Defense) sinks into a victim's dream-body and prevents them from leaving the Temenos by any means. It can only be removed by a Master of Mind or a sufficiently powerful Archetype of Rank 4+ using its Influence, almost always in exchange for an onerous favor. Castellans and Rocs are not powerful enough, but Garuda (or Naga) might be, as are entities in other Temenos realms.<br /> <br /> They use the Bubble and other magics to trap more experienced mages and ransom them for rotes and Tass and sympathetic names, among other resources useful to an impoverished mystical faction. If they were presented with concrete information about the fallen Legacy linked to &quot;their&quot; realm, they might be willing to share their combat and dueling lore or some of their unique Astral rotes, but they jealously guard their secret knowledge of Dharmakshetra itself.<br /> <br /> Some Mystagogues who have studied the Dreamhounds find it unbelievable that such a marginal and scattered Nameless faction could independently be drawn to the realm and develop the magical expertise to create their own rotes. They believe that the Dreamhounds are simply pawns of a more powerful entity: perhaps Naga, or perhaps something stranger. On the other hand, the Diamond believes a lot of things about the Nameless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mystery Cult Initiation: Dreamhounds</b><br /> \u2022: one dot of the Dream Merit<br /> \u2022\u2022: one dot of a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988166-expanded-duel-arcane-rules\">Duel Arcane Merit</a><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Rote Specialties in Brawl, Occult, and Weaponry<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: three dot Astral Adept Merit, activated by performing a repetitive <i>kata </i>until entering a meditative trance </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:09:03-07:00","id":989481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988390-temenos-realm-dharmakshetra-and-the-duel-goetic?p=988478#post988478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the description of the realm. Lots of potential story hooks hiding in there, from finding a thing hidden on the site to finding connections to other strange realms.<br /> <br /> (Don't honestly care about the weird dueling rules, much, so I just skimmed them. No offense or anything---Just didn't hook me. I suppose that's feedback, too...)<br /> <br /> The Naga/Garuda duel is pretty slick. I would watch that.<br /> (Ho, okay: Imagine a Free Councilor who saw this and thought that it was both edifying and awesome to watch, so set about to stream it live. There's a weird plot hook, even if the two dueling don't actually care, since other magi almost certainly would be offended. Another would be to find out which parts fit which party's dominion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like! I really like the image of streaming the battle too, it reminds me of the Free Council book cover art. I'll remember that when this comes up in my game. My PCs have already tried to upload one magical throwdown to WorldStar.<br /> <br /> The original impetus for putting this together was to have an excuse for my weird dueling rules, but the rest of it has kind of become more interesting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T17:40:37-07:00","id":989628,"title":"","content":"I <i>do</i> like that weird dueling is in-theme for the realm. <br /> <br /> Something to consider:<br /> <br /> If this realm's theme is dueling, it might stand to reason that events in the realm tend to the dramatic---Harder to control one's self, and all that. (Not sure how best to display that, but a hit to Composure might serve.)<br /> <br /> Maybe a hit to Compsure with a bump to Resolve if you're aligned with rocs and the reverse if you align with the nag.<br /> <br /> (Just spit-balling.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}